    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>New package: gr-satellites 5.9.0, a GNU Radio out-of-tree module with
telemetry decoders for around 400 amateur satellites.

gnuradio is already in Factory (3.10.12.0) and its devel project is
hardware:sdr, which is where this package is maintained, so it sits next to
the gr-osmosdr and gr-iqbal out-of-tree modules Factory already ships.

Cleaned up before submitting:

- Source now comes from the upstream release tag archive. It previously came
  from a manual tar_scm service, so the committed tarball was not something
  OBS or a reviewer could reproduce; the _service is gone. The tag archive
  also leaves out the satellite-recordings submodule, 66MB of sample captures
  that only the manual test.sh uses and that nothing in the build, install or
  payload touches.
- License corrected from GPL-3.0-only. libgnuradio-satellites also links MIT
  (lib/randomizer.c), Apache-2.0 (lib/viterbi/, vendored from xukmin/viterbi)
  and LGPL code (lib/libfec/ and lib/viterbi.c, Karn). Karn's headers say only
  &quot;LGPL&quot; with no version; I tagged LGPL-2.1-or-later because -only would be
  GPL-3-incompatible inside this very library, and left a Legal-Review-Notice
  above the tag flagging it as an open question rather than settling it.
  Debian reads the same headers as LGPL-2.1. Both licence texts are shipped.
- Runtime dependencies were badly under-declared. satellites/__init__.py
  imports the submitter and csp_zmq modules unconditionally, so requests,
  websocket-client and pyzmq are hard requirements; gnuradio, PyYAML, numpy
  and matplotlib (for the shipped smog_p_spectrum) were missing too. construct
  is floored at 2.9 per upstream's install docs, and feh is recommended for
  the realtime image decoders.
- devel now pulls the library subpackage plus gnuradio-devel, whose headers
  and cmake config it reaches into.
- Python bytecode is now shipped (upstream's cmake installed none), with
  fdupes for the identical .pyc/.opt-1.pyc pairs.
- CRLF conversion moved from the buildroot into %prep, where it also covers
  satyaml/EIRSAT-1.yml that the previous glob missed.
- Shebangs stripped from the installed python modules, which are importable
  modules rather than scripts.
- gnuradio BuildRequires floored at 3.10 per the CMakeLists find_package.

No %check: upstream declares no C++ tests, and all 29 of its python QA tests
set GR_TEST_PYTHON_DIRS to the build tree plus a 3.8-era swig directory, where
no importable satellites package exists, so they cannot run out of tree. The
reason is recorded in a spec comment. Upstream CI does not run them either and
Debian runs them with failures ignored.

rpmlint is clean, 0 errors and 0 badness. The one filter in the rpmlintrc
covers explicit-lib-dependency on python3-matplotlib, which is a false
positive: a python import dependency cannot be autodetected, so the explicit
Requires is correct.

I have added myself (pluskalm) as a co-maintainer of the package in
hardware:sdr, alongside the existing maintainer.</comment>
